Data Scientist (various positions)
$$$ Negotiable
7 + 12 Month ContractOur client, a large Federal Government Department are seeking various Data Scientists for a long 7 + 12 month contract based in any capital city or worked remotely.
The Data Scientists will be:
Assessing the nature of labour market recovery;
Determining skills shortages or surplus;
Analysing the structural shifts that are occurring in the labour market, and
Identifying current, emerging and future skills needs.The Data Scientists will have:
Demonstrated experience in applying data science to meet the needs of business users, including understanding business requirements, articulating problem statements and developing criteria for suitable implementation of data science solutions;
Demonstrated knowledge of appropriate techniques to explore, profile and cleanse data from a diverse range of sources and experience in presenting exploratory data analysis to non-technical stakeholders;
Experience using Python, PySpark, R or SparkR programming languages through development environments including Databricks for developing supervised and unsupervised machine learning models, with a particular emphasis on Natural Language Processing, and
Demonstrated experience in using data science preferably for economic research, working with Australian Labour Market data such as ABS Quarterly Labour Force Survey and Census.If you would like to apply for this contract opportunity, please click the Apply for This Job button. Alternatively, you may call Ronald on (02) 6299 1006, quoting Job # 4092.
Please note: this role closes on Tuesday 27th of October.

At yourtown, we believe every young person has the right to a brighter future and aim to be part of the solution by delivering services that get results. Our services include Kids Helpline, training and employment services, parent education and specialist accommodation for families.
Reporting to the Data and Performance Manager, the Lead Data Scientist will support the data analysis and service/program performance reporting services for yourtown to contribute to improving the delivery of quality services for clients, and development of evidence-based practice. You will also:
Lead the collection, analysis and reporting on program and service performance and trend data to support yourtown’s services and programs and strategic priorities;
Lead performance analysis and reporting including the production of reports for relevant internal and external stakeholders, including government agencies;
Overseas high-quality data and statistical analysis;
Overseas the design and development of advance modelling analysis, using machine learning and AI;
Develops custom visualisations and simple web applications;
Lead the maintenance, cleansing and continuous improvement of yourtown’s data;
Provide effective and meaningful leadership and management of junior staff;
Provide options for analysis and provided meaningful reasons for analysis choices;
Ensure high-quality data and understand how data is generated out experimental design and how these experiments can produce actionable, trustworthy conclusions;
Assist senior management in making key business decisions; and
Work across yourtown to build tools for data tasks that will accelerate and automate workflows.
Role requirements:
Bachelor level qualification, PhD or Master preferred, in data analytics, data science or other discipline relevant to data analysis and a minimum of five years’ relevant experience;
An expert in either Python or R;
An expert in SQL;
Strong numerical skills and a good understanding of statistics, performance reporting and the use of statistical techniques to interpret and understand data;
A demonstrated ability to lead the development and implementation of machine learning and AI based methodologies;
Demonstrated ability to use data cloud-based data platforms, like Azure or AWS;
A demonstrated ability to use the Microsoft Office suite of software at a high level to perform and present analytics;
Lead the creation of engaging analytics using data visualisation software like Power BI , Tableau or have the ability to produce your own data visualisations using R or Python;
High level written and oral communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to engage with a wide audience and a range of internal and external stakeholders; and
Good judgement and the ability to be resilient and adaptable while maintaining accuracy and consistency in data reporting.
Please submit a cover letter (max 2 pages) with your application that demonstrates your experience against the selection criteria.
For full position description please visit: https://careers.yourtown.com.au/
About yourtown:
At yourtown, we believe every young person has the right to a brighter future and aim to be part of the solution by delivering services that get results. Our services include Kids Helpline, training and employment services for young people, parent education and specialist accommodation for families. We are one of the largest not-for-profit providers of services for young people in Australia with sites across Queensland, New South Wales, South Australia and Tasmania. The community with yourtown’s Art Unions funds most of what we do. At yourtown you will be part of the solution.
We offer attractive employment conditions including access to salary packaging arrangements and paid parental leave. Find your place at yourtown.
Contact: Breanna Buyers, Talent Acquisition Specialist on 0466 471 023
yourtown is committed to providing services that protect and keep children, young people and adults at risk free from harm. The appointment of successful applicants will be subject to satisfactory screening for child-related employment including the completion of a National Criminal History Check and retention of a valid Working with Children Check.
"In our team we value diversity, inclusivity and people who want to make a difference"
www.yourtown.com.au
